## Where things are

<!-- The routing block. Names a PATH and a TRIGGER, never a summary of contents — a summary
     is a second copy of the file, and restatement across files is how contradictions are
     born. These files cost nothing at startup; only these lines do. -->

Read these when the trigger applies. Do not read them by default.

- `docs/project/SPEC.md` — product scope and locked constraints. Read before changing what
  the product does or promises.
- `docs/project/PLAN.md` — active milestones and acceptance gates. Read before starting work.
- `docs/project/STATUS.md` — current state and blockers. Read at session start if resuming.
- `docs/project/decisions/` — one decision each, immutable. Read the relevant record before
  reversing an architectural choice.
- `docs/project/pitfalls.md` — verified failed approaches. Read before choosing an approach
  in an area where a previous attempt failed.
- `docs/research/` — evidence, not truth. Never a constraint until promoted.

